#
# aria2c deliverable — handed in as a binary artifact.
# NOT downloaded. NOT built during a normal IRIS build.
#
# Rebuilt 2026-10-13 from the preserved p11 source plus pinned patch 0012.
# Patches 0001 through 0012; required hybrid peer TLS is explicitly opt-in
# and requires fresh certificate-identity withdrawal data. Default is disabled.
# OpenSSL 3.5.8, native x86_64 / QEMU aarch64. Both exact clients passed
# identity-withdrawal TLS, fragmented TLS collision, handshake, peer-cap,
# capped tracker-control and transfer checks. Extracted p12 source rebuilt
# both hashes with cached build layers and locked offline APKs.
# Emulation is not device performance proof.
# Local development artifacts; this record does not assert a published release.
#
# aria2-next version : 2.5.6
# source pin         : d4971f0e12322e2ffcdb1721911b7d5c6206d0e5
# patches applied    : 12
#   - 0001-getpeers-keys-filter.patch
#   - 0002-fix-uaf-peer-blocklist-disconnect.patch
#   - 0003-fix-pkcs12-chain-type-confusion.patch
#   - 0004-fix-ed2k-iterator-invalidation.patch
#   - 0005-hard-bt-max-peers.patch
#   - 0006-preserve-coalesced-bt-handshake.patch
#   - 0007-seeder-goodbye-grace.patch
#   - 0008-required-hybrid-peer-tls.patch
#   - 0009-test-seeder-goodbye-grace.patch
#   - 0010-resolve-crossed-peer-handshakes.patch
#   - 0011-withdraw-peer-identities.patch
#   - 0012-isolate-tracker-control-throttle.patch
#
# tools/get-aria2c.sh verifies the handed-in binary against these
